---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import SeoNav from '../../components/SeoNav.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Share preview"
	lede="Three pages with deliberately different head metadata, so every rule can be seen firing and passing."
	seo={{
		description:
			'Fixtures for the share preview: a fully tagged page, a page that trips several audit rules at once, and a page with nothing but a title.',
		image: '/og/undersized.png',
		imageSize: [800, 418],
		imageAlt: 'Abstract share card, deliberately too small for a wide card',
	}}
>
	<Callout title="What to try" tone="accent">
		Open a chat window and press <strong>◉</strong> in its toolbar. The sheet
		reads this page's head and shows what each network renders. Then walk the
		four pages below and watch the cards and the issue list change.
	</Callout>

	<SeoNav />

	<Callout title="This page is the middle tier">
		Its <code>og:image</code> is 800×418 — big enough that every network keeps
		it, too small for the wide card, which the preview reports as one warning
		rather than an error. The other three pages sit either side of that.
	</Callout>

	<section class="panel" aria-label="What each fixture demonstrates">
		<h2>What each page is for</h2>
		<dl>
			<dt>Clean</dt>
			<dd>
				Every tag present and within limits: absolute <code>og:image</code> at
				1200×630 with declared dimensions and alt text,
				<code>twitter:card</code> set to <code>summary_large_image</code>,
				<code>og:url</code> matching the canonical link. The preview finds
				nothing to report, and every card renders its wide image.
			</dd>

			<dt>Broken</dt>
			<dd>
				Several real mistakes at once: an <code>og:image</code> written as a
				relative path that no crawler can follow, and which is 64×64 anyway; an
				invalid <code>twitter:card</code> value; an <code>og:url</code> that
				disagrees with the canonical link; a title and description past the
				lengths Google reads; and <code>noindex</code>.
			</dd>

			<dt>Bare head</dt>
			<dd>
				A title and nothing else — no description, no Open Graph, no
				<code>twitter:</code> tags, no canonical, no favicon, and no
				<code>lang</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>. Every card falls back to
				the document title and renders without an image, which is what a page
				nobody has tagged actually looks like when shared.
			</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>

	<Callout title="Fixing from here">
		On the Issues tab, <strong>Fix with AI</strong> sends one finding — or the
		whole list — to the agent along with the current tag values, and the chat
		opens with the route attached. The head tags for these pages live in
		<code>src/components/Seo.astro</code>, driven by the
		<code>seo</code> prop each page passes to the layout.
	</Callout>
</Layout>

<style>
	.panel {
		border: 1px dashed #3f4552;
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
	}

	h2 {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
	}

	dl {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin: 0;
	}

	dt {
		color: #c4b5fd;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	dd {
		color: #aeb6c5;
		margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
	}

	code {
		color: #c4b5fd;
	}
</style>
